cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Sleep Scoring App: Interactive review and correction of rodent sleep annotations with synchronized electrophysiology, photometry, and behavior video"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Yue
    family-names: Zhao
    affiliation: "University of Rochester, Rochester, NY, USA"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0819-5012"
abstract: >-
  A local desktop application for reviewing and correcting rodent sleep
  annotations (wakefulness, NREM sleep, REM sleep, and microarousals) at
  one-second resolution. It brings EEG, EMG, an EEG spectrogram, an optional
  fiber-photometry norepinephrine (NE) signal, and behavior-video clips of a
  selected interval into one shared scoring workflow. Users can label
  intervals manually or generate automatic scores, then revise individual
  seconds or whole bouts; labels a user has supplied are kept as-is in every
  automatic result. The default automatic scorer is a rule-based algorithm
  that adapts to expert-labeled examples: it treats the user's labels on the
  current recording as ground truth and adjusts its parameters to best match
  them. The externally developed sDREAMER model can be selected instead, with
  optional PyTorch dependencies. Completed scores are saved back to the
  recording and exported as bout tables with stage and transition statistics.
repository-code: "https://github.com/yzhaoinuw/sleep_scoring"
# Zenodo concept DOI. It resolves to the newest release, so it stays correct
